  "explicit_limitations": [
    "Oracle-gated evaluation: the evaluator holds the gold answer, supplies repair hints on FAIL, and stops on PASS; results govern systems with reliable external feedback rather than intrinsic self-correction or costly/noisy verification.",
    "Post-freeze exploratory status: both the main RF-with-feedback comparison and the 400-problem forced-submission run (one actor, one domain, single run removing the whole gate) were added after the pre-registration freeze.",
    "Pre-registered endpoints: P4 (actor x enforcement interaction) returned null after Holm correction with uninformative power on Llama-3.3 contrasts; P1a failed as written and was re-scoped to answer authorship.",
    "Logging & scoring defects disclosed: 75.7% of gpt-oss RF messages lost hidden reasoning in logs; automated runner graded last submitted answer while recording last held answer (17% disagreement on gemma-4 Omni-MATH RS failed runs, shifting verdict-matched RS-RF from +0.009 to +0.029 [+0.004, +0.054]).",
    "Evaluator overlap & domain scope: gpt-oss-120b served as both one of the three studied actors and the universal evaluator; benchmarks are restricted to text-only mathematical and scientific reasoning."
  ],
